   "text": "### Summary\n\n* **Compatibility:** `bloomery-serve` uses the llama-server HTTP API, meaning OpenAI and Anthropic clients work unchanged. It supports chat completions, tool calls, reasoning, and token counting.\n* **Model Loading:** It automatically handles model placement across GPUs and CPUs. It supports GGUF files and Hugging Face repositories via `--hf`.\n* **Performance:** It uses speculative decoding (MTP/DSpark) and adaptive residency to move experts between GPU and CPU for better speed.\n* **Hardware:** Requires sm_86+ GPUs (e.g., RTX 3090/A6000) and NVIDIA driver R580+. It manages memory carefully to avoid OOM crashes.\n* **Features:** Supports image input for V4.1, a decision seat for agent tool selection, and API key authentication.\n* **Limits:** Currently supports one model per server and one expert tier card. Context limits vary by model (e.g., GLM-5.3 is limited to 16,384 positions).\n* **Evaluation:** Users are encouraged to compare performance against llama-server using the same model file and settings.\n\n### Three Settings You Are Most Likely to Need\n\n1. **`--hf <repo>[:<quant>]`**: To specify the model you want to run (e.g., `unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL`).\n2. **`--parallel N`**: To control the number of concurrent requests (slots) the server can handle.\n3. **`--ctx-size`**: To set the maximum context length for the model."
  },
