   "text": "### Summary\n\n* **Compatibility:** `bloomery-serve` uses the llama-server HTTP API, meaning OpenAI and Anthropic clients work unchanged. It supports chat completions, tool calls, reasoning, and image input (V4.1).\n* **Hardware:** Requires sm_86+ GPUs and NVIDIA driver R580+. It supports one model per server and automatic GPU placement.\n* **Memory Management:** It automatically splits models across GPU and CPU RAM. It also supports NVMe tiering for overflow and adaptive residency to move experts between host and card.\n* **Performance:** Supports speculative decoding via MTP (Qwen3.8, GLM-5.3) and DSpark (V4.1). It allows concurrent requests via `--parallel`.\n* **Security:** Supports API keys via `--api-key` or `--api-key-file`. The server binds to localhost by default.\n* **Control:** Can be stopped via signals (`SIGINT`) or the `/shutdown` HTTP endpoint.\n* **Evaluation:** A checklist is provided for users to benchmark the server against llama-server using the same models and settings.\n* **Future:** Work is ongoing for multi-card support and new model architectures.\n\n### Three Settings Most Likely Needed\n\n1. **`--hf <repo>[:<quant>]`**: To specify the model to download and serve (e.g., `unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL`).\n2. **`--parallel N`**: To control the number of concurrent requests/slots the server can handle.\n3. **`--ctx-size`**: To set the maximum context window size for the model."
  }
